{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1509675-sidereal-artifact-wolf-in-fox-s-clothing","id":1509675,"title":"Sidereal Artifact: Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T19:07:18-07:00","id":1509675,"title":"Sidereal Artifact: Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing","content":"Suggestions or advice appreciated, this is very much a work in progress. I'd like further Evocations to split into two trees, one for each armour, but I'm not sure what to put in them.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing</b> <i>Starmetal (Silken Armour / Lamellar Armour)</i><br /> <br /> The Arcane Fate is a brutal curse to all but the most antisocial of Sidereals, denying them long-term companionship outside of very narrow exceptions. Nu-e Foxfire, Maiden of Maybe, spun this set of armour as one of many attempts to circumvent being entirely forgotten by the world. Born of Wyld-shaped Starmetal and discarded threads off of the Loom of Fate itself, the Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing can -just barely- hold Fate at bay. While not perfect, it was the most successful solution the Harbinger has achieved to date.<br /> <br /> The Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing is a dualistic thing, a Starmetal-infused ensemble that can be willed to flicker between two distinct forms and associated &quot;personalities&quot;. While any Exalt can attune to it and make use of this shifting, only those suffering from the Arcane Fate can truly benefit.<br /> <br /> The Fox is a hooded d\u014dgi of black silk, tied at the waist with a scarlet obi and embroidered at the hem with patterns of gold and crimson flowers. A smiling fox mask of Starmetal-inlaid alibaster covers the wearer's face, the metalic patterns throwing up a rainbow shimmer with every movement. When in combat and wearing this guise, the owner feels most comfortable using Dreaming Pearl Courtisan or Black Claw Style.<br /> <br /> The Wolf is a terrible carapace of red-lacquered Starmetal and black cloth, wrought to look like flames, flayed flesh, and exposed muscles. A demonic canine mask covers the wearer's face, crimson framed by a mane of grey hair. When in combat and wearing this guise, the owner feels most comfortable using Fire Dragon or Steel Devil Style. (Think Monster Hunter World's Odogaron armour.)<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing</b><br /> When attuning to Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing, the wearer unlocks Two-Faced Terror for free.<br /> <br /> <i>Two-Faced Terror</i><br /> <u>Cost</u>: 1m; <u>Mins</u>: Essence 1<br /> <u>Type</u>: Reflexive<br /> <u>Keywords</u>: None<br /> <u>Duration</u>: Instant<br /> <u>Prerequisites</u>: None<br /> <br /> Spend a mote, switch between Silken Armour (The Fox) and a Lamellar Armour set (The Wolf)<br /> <br /> <i>Resonant</i> - each armour mode can hold one Resplendent Destiny, which the owner designs when purchasing this Evocation and automatically enters when wearing it. The destinies are immune to erosion, are unique to each owner, and persist unless the owner gives up metaphysical ownership of the armour. That is, theft would not void the true owner's stored Destinies, nor does loaning it out, but giving the armour away would. Each destiny must conform to certain themes: The Wolf craves violence, terror, and speed. The Fox craves grace, seduction, and stealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Smiles Skin Deep</i><br /> <u>Cost</u>: -; <u>Mins</u>: Essence 1<br /> <u>Type</u>: Permanent<br /> <u>Keywords</u>: None<br /> <u>Duration</u>: Permanent<br /> <u>Prerequisites:</u> Two-Faced Terror<br /> <br /> While wearing Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing, the owner gains the following benefits depending it's current form:<br /> <br /> The Wolf: Characters perceive The Wolf as their<br /> natural predator, and an unpredictably rabid one at that. She seems a mob leg breaker to a gambler, or a looting soldier to a peasant.<br /> <br /> The Fox: The Fox carries a paradoxical air of insignificance and mystique, a harmless curiosity that should be approached with cautious reverence so as to not startle.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the form, the wearer can leverage these impressions as though it were a Minor Intimacy. However, that Intimacy applies to <i>all</i> interactions undertaken while wearing the armour. Attempting peaceful negotiations while wearing The Wolf, for example, would be exceptionally difficult in most cases, as would attempting to intimidate someone while wearing The Fox.<br /> <br /> Characters who already have an applicable Intimacy towards The Fox or The Wolf treat that as being one level higher.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Kaleidoscope-Fox Flare</i><br /> <u>Cost</u>: 2m; <u>Mins</u>: Essence 1 <u>Type</u>: Reflexive<br /> <u>Keywords</u>: None<br /> <u>Duration</u>: One scene<br /> <u>Prerequisite</u>: Smiles Skin Deep<br /> <br /> The Fox's Starmetal markings shimmer in hypnotic patterns, astrological auroras that inexorably draw the eye. Her influence rolls ignore multiple target penalties, and she adds two non-charm successes to attempts to instill fascination or reverence.<br /> <br /> Shifting to The Wolf or removing the armour causes this Evocation to end early.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Cruel-Clawed Howl</i><br /> <u>Cost</u>: 4m; <u>Mins</u>: , Essence 1<br /> <u>Type</u>: Supplemental<br /> <u>Keywords</u>: None<br /> <u>Duration</u>: Instant<br /> <u>Prerequisites</u>: Smiles Skin Deep <br /> <br /> The Wolf\u2019s ferocity tests the will of even the most<br /> courageous. She adds (higher of Essence or 3) dice on a threaten roll or on an inspire roll to create fear. Her targets can\u2019t use Intimacies expressing courage or fearlessness to bolster Resolve against the roll or to resist it in a Decision Point.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><i>Potential Fox Track </i></u>- benefit or ability for The Fox. Not-my-problem field? Hypnotic patterns, ala Peacock Shadow Eyes? Rainbow-burst smoke bomb vanishing?<br /> <br /> <u><i>Potential Wolf Track</i></u> - benefit or ability for The Wolf. Cause enemies to route? Cause DoT or crippling effects? Upgrade the Intimacy strength for Smiles Skin Deep?<br /> <br /> <br /> Capstone idea? - can only be learned by Sidereals, combines The Fox and The Wolf into a single RD when not wearing the armour. As long as they own the Wolf-In-Fox's-Clothing, they've beaten the Arcane Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-30-2023, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T08:48:24-07:00","id":1510087,"title":"","content":"If the theme is about having two additional somewhat more reliable resplendent destinies, how about for 2a (the fox one) a penalty to the target's ability to resist stealth, seduction, and/or grace themed actions for intimacies the target holds towards the fox RD, and for 2b penalizing the target's ability to resist violence, terror, or speed associated actions based on the target's intimacies for the wolf? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T03:18:42-07:00","id":1510182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1509675-sidereal-artifact-wolf-in-fox-s-clothing?p=1510087#post1510087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the theme is about having two additional somewhat more reliable resplendent destinies, how about for 2a (the fox one) a penalty to the target's ability to resist stealth, seduction, and/or grace themed actions for intimacies the target holds towards the fox RD, and for 2b penalizing the target's ability to resist violence, terror, or speed associated actions based on the target's intimacies for the wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically <u>Predator and Prey Mirror</u> from the Lunar Charmset? It's a good idea, but may as well be a single charm like PPM, with the effect changing with the form-shift.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for other Evocations? I'm thinking maybe stuff like forcefully giving targets relevant Intimacies for each form... maybe only lasting for the scene? I can probably load The Wolf with straight-up combat modifier tricks, and The Fox with social and stealth tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T04:01:15-07:00","id":1510184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1509675-sidereal-artifact-wolf-in-fox-s-clothing?p=1510182#post1510182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically <u>Predator and Prey Mirror</u> from the Lunar Charmset? It's a good idea, but may as well be a single charm like PPM, with the effect changing with the form-shift.</div> </div> </div> </div> That charm gives the target temporary intimacies. I was thinking that because the theme of your armor is creating non-decaying resplendent destinies, you could get a benefit for intimacies that the target has for the two identities of the armor. This furthers what I took to be the desire for the character to really dive in to being the fox and being the wolf, now they have more motivation to do so.<br /> <br /> Yes, I could imagine it being only a single charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T04:09:19-07:00","id":1510186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1509675-sidereal-artifact-wolf-in-fox-s-clothing?p=1510184#post1510184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That charm gives the target temporary intimacies. I was thinking that because the theme of your armor is creating non-decaying resplendent destinies, you could get a benefit for intimacies that the target has for the two identities of the armor. This furthers what I took to be the desire for the character to really dive in to being the fox and being the wolf, now they have more motivation to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've interpreted my intent correctly, my solution for now is to make a PPM equivalent that's always on while wearing one of the forms. That is, The Wolf is always treated as if the people it interacts with have a Minor Tie of Fear or an equivalent impression, while The Fox gives a Minor Tie of Fascination (or something similar, can't quite articulate the emotion for The Fox). Downside is, of course, that you can't turn that <i>off </i>unless you switch forms or take the armour off entirely, which switches the Destiny.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}